The files above copied from models.json are its
`model_messages.instructions_template` values, deduplicated byte for byte. The
two compact files are Codex's local-compaction prompt and the prefix it puts
before the model's summary. The Apache License 2.0 text is in LICENSE.

The freeform apply_patch grammar in assets/codex/apply_patch.lark is copied
byte for byte from OpenAI Codex, commit
ca21fe65d18a9b6326759fb4263c65dfbb645aa5:

  assets/codex/apply_patch.lark
    codex-rs/core/assets/tools/apply_patch.lark

The exact freeform tool description sent by the bridge is copied from
codex-rs/core/src/tools/handlers/apply_patch_spec.rs in that commit. That code
is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The review-agent skill under skills/review-agent/ is adapted from OpenAI Codex,
commit ca21fe65d18a9b6326759fb4263c65dfbb645aa5:

  skills/review-agent/SKILL.md
    codex-rs/skills/src/assets/samples/review-agent/SKILL.md

The review methodology, checklist and result format are Codex's. The file is
adapted for DSH rather than copied: its tool guidance names the DSH tools the
review uses, and Codex's agents/openai.yaml interface metadata is not carried
over. That code is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The apply_patch parser and text updater under src/patch/ are a TypeScript port
of OpenAI Codex, commit ca21fe65d18a9b6326759fb4263c65dfbb645aa5. The port
follows the upstream logic function by function; comments and module docs were
written for this package rather than copied.

  src/patch/parser.ts
    codex-rs/apply-patch/src/parser.rs
    codex-rs/apply-patch/src/streaming_parser.rs
  src/patch/seek-sequence.ts
    codex-rs/apply-patch/src/seek_sequence.rs
  src/patch/text-file.ts
    codex-rs/apply-patch/src/text_file.rs
  src/patch/file-update.ts
    codex-rs/apply-patch/src/file_update.rs
